<title>FINLAND: SAMPO BUYS COMPUTERS FOR FIM 20 MLN.</title>
<headline>SAMPO BUYS COMPUTERS FOR FIM 20 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish insurer Sampo group said in a statement on Wednesday it had ordered new workstations and systems for 20 million markka as part of a broad project to reorganise customer services.</p>
<p>The workstations would be delivered by Fujitsu's ICL Data and the Compaq server environment would be delivered by Facidata.</p>
<p>&quot;The new equipment will be installed all over the country in the autumn,&quot; Sampo said.  &quot;The value of the deliveries is over 20 million markka,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 242</p>
</text>
